    <div class=3D"s-prose js-post-body" itemprop=3D"text">
<p>You can use <a href=3D"https://gpac.wp.mines-telecom.fr/downloads/gpac-n=
ightly-builds" rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer">MP4Box 0.6.2-DEV-rev453</a> (May=
 2016) or higher to do this:</p>
<pre><code>mp4box -add alfa.mp4 -add bravo.srt:txtflags=3D0xC0000000 -new c=
harlie.mp4
</code></pre>
<p><a href=3D"https://github.com/svnpenn/a/blob/af30667/etc/mp4box.sh#L27-L=
28" rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer">Example</a></p>
<p>This will mark the subtitle stream in the output file as forced.</p>
<p><strong>However</strong>, this mark will only be recognized starting wit=
h these versions of
programs:</p>
<ul>
<li><p><a href=3D"https://nightly.mpc-hc.org/" rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer">=
MPC-HC 1.7.10.207</a> (May 2016)</p>
</li>
<li><p><a href=3D"https://nightlies.videolan.org/" rel=3D"nofollow noreferr=
er">VLC media player 3.0.0-20161101</a> (Nov 2016)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<p>I have seen mentions to <a href=3D"https://ffmpeg.org/pipermail/ffmpeg-d=
evel/2015-January/167371.html" rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer">this post</a> on=
 the FFmpeg mailing list about a
patch that implements disposition for FFmpeg:</p>
<pre><code>ffmpeg -i alfa.mp4 -i bravo.srt -c copy -c:s mov_text -dispositi=
on:s forced charlie.mp4
</code></pre>
<p>However after having tried it with both "forced" and "default", the subt=
itles
marked by FFmpeg are not recognized as forced by either MPC-HC or VLC.</p>
    </div>
